    930  fcb9							; --- Phase 3: phase-cell blink (PF buffer pokes) ----------------------
    931  fcb9							; Body moved after the level data (PhaseBlink, ~130B — the StageBandTab
    932  fcb9							; window $F3C4..$F4C4 was full; the data window has the only free
    933  fcb9							; hole). Contract: clobbers A/X/Y/FetchPtr/RectCount/LineCount/
    934  fcb9							; CollisionCellX/CollisionEndY ($8F scratch — the pack below rebuilds
    935  fcb9							; it). The PF buffers ARE the collision map (cell walk + laser read
    936  fcb9							; them) — toggling the cell's two bits THERE makes render + PHM +
    937  fcb9							; laser follow with zero kernel cost. 64f full cycle = EnemyRamP bit5
    938  fcb9							; (32 on + 32 off; clock-derived, no state bytes — locked plan).
    939  fcb9							; --- PhaseBlink ping-pong (chunk A2): it MUST run after the band/ball
    940  fcb9							; staging above and before the pack below (the crunch walk overwrites
    941  fcb9							; Temp/BandTab for its cell — running it earlier let SBT's own staging
    942  fcb9							; erase the crunch mask, and every crunch kill stopped latching).
